{"accepted_ir_sha256":"sha256:c238963bf7d59f43689dbdc2ed3645651f98a40556208677a5b78d4d56d548f0","auditor":"root/tier2_semantics_audit","bridge_two_builds_status":"PASS_REPORTED_BY_BOUND_REGISTERED_CERTIFICATE","build_report_hashes":["sha256:925bef304bff06da5de6e8346c9d991500e6e5156ab63025d3358b17b054fb0e","sha256:925bef304bff06da5de6e8346c9d991500e6e5156ab63025d3358b17b054fb0e"],"checked_observations":["Exact delivered bytes, bridge input bytes, sourceBytes literal, implementation IR and source descriptor all agree on the same 813-byte program.","The program has exactly one entry solve(Input)->Int, no helpers, and the complete signed floor-sum body over the n-element natural range. Its four fields all remain Int.","SourceParses and SourceChecks are included in EdgeProp. checkedProgram and entry_solve are tied to successful compileProgram and exact findEntry equalities, so fallback defaults cannot discharge the bridge.","source_fn_solve is the decoded result of the compiled entry run on the complete input adapter; it is not the accepted reference definition or a separately supplied model.","Refines_solve quantifies universally over every accepted Input with no extra hypothesis. The submitted proof unfolds the actual compiler function and proves this equality by kernel reflexivity.","The Int adapter is identity; the record adapter preserves all n,m,a,b components in canonical ordered products and has both typed inverse laws. Exact record RawLaws derive from the four-field RecordLayout and Int/product/unit laws.","RawEval_solve connects normative raw evalEntry to encoded compiled results, and InputsCover_solve covers every ArgsTyped raw argument list by an accepted Input, using decode/encode inverse laws. Neither condition is restricted to positive a/b or a finite set of inputs.","SourceAdequate_solve is tied to compileProgram, findEntry, exact parameter/result RawLaws and typed coverage. The frozen SourceFacts module supplies actual normative observation laws for totality, determinism, preserved input, empty effects, pure data and restricted runtime.","O1/O2 transfer retains the complete original universal valid_input domain and signed floor-sum value formula, conjoined with the exact accepted source boundary. S1/S2 transfer retains the same actual source boundary.","EdgeProp requires parsing, checking, input coverage, raw evaluation, universal refinement, SourceFactsAdequate and all four per-ID transfers in a single conjunction.","The semantic certificate binds the exact accepted IR, accepted theorem statement hashes, source/proof/model/profile/relation, goal, implementation IR and accepted bridge modules. All referenced hashes were checked.","The registered semantic checker reports two isolated bridge builds A/B, zero sorries/errors, matching exports/module hashes/propositions and only allowed proof axioms. No new kernel replay was launched by this passive audit.","The current finite claim graph requires END_TO_END_VERIFIED for O1/O2/S1/S2 with the semantic edge, declaration implementation/link, per-ID implementation/link/proof and all four closure premises. Native LINKED PASS evidence exists for D1 and all four guarantees."],"concrete_scope_defects":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T18:15:01.916922+00:00","end_to_end_status":"NOT_ASSIGNED_BY_THIS_RECEIPT","exclusions":["No hidden case, oracle, old task solution or prior candidate was used.","No production/frozen-cohort edit, model call, widened test campaign or author/controller feedback occurred.","This interim receipt grants no terminal or end-to-end milestone."],"format":"verislop.independent-implementation-scope-audit/0.1","goal_sha256":"sha256:ff6790b25e33d8831006c657a49636643b7c59207fcd931f05186ad29ec9711f","implementation_ir_sha256":"sha256:139491ca90a1ab93680cc477a398b0148d6471da0ed1fb67706170187e6e3217","independent_kernel_replay_status":"NOT_RUN","manifest":[{"path":"captured/request/revised-prompt.txt","sha256":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302